{
  "artifact": "mindmake-approved-production-routes-r22",
  "recordedAt": "2026-09-24",
  "status": "Owner-approved page-body redesign of /case-studies, merged onto the r21 action-bar line. The owner reviewed rendered desktop and phone frames across several rounds on 24 September 2026 and directed it to production.",
  "scopeRequested": "Merge the two renderings of the eight client records on /case-studies into one surface, remove the duplicate archive without losing anything it carried, and design the phone as its own composition.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "The trailing slash is a real page, not a test spelling. Vercel resolves /ai-brain and /ai-brain/ to the same document, so a visitor arriving at either had to get the same bar; keying on the exact pathname meant they did not, and React tore the route down to client rendering. Normalised rather than special-cased.",
    "src/test/action-bar-door.test.ts locks it at the server render, with a negative control: reverted to the exact-pathname lookup, its two trailing-slash cases fail and the other nine pass.",
    "The phone loses the door rather than the footer. A second row put the bar at 150.7px on a 568px screen, over a quarter of it, and its own reserve then covered the last footer link. The bar's job on a phone is the one action, and the menu carries both routes one tap away.",
    "CASE-PROOF-FIELD-S3: /case-studies rendered the same eight records twice, splitting each in half — the field carried the claim, a separate archive a page below carried the testimony and the only diagram bound to the record. Merged into one surface. Attribution on every cold tile, the client quote and StoryFigureView in the open record, a close control where a reader looks for one. mechanismGlyph removed on the evidence of a rendered bake-off across all eight records. The archive is unmounted, not deleted, in src/components/mindmake/SourceRecords.tsx. Page height falls from 4271px to 2401px at 1440x900 and from 5704px to 2522px at 390x844.",
    "The phone is a separate composition: a full-bleed horizontal snap rail, one whole record per screen, no expansion step. Titles, quotes and figures are declared bands with a floor, aligned to 0px at 320, 360, 390, 411 and 430, and free to grow when a reader enlarges their text. Landscape gets two columns. Nothing between a thumb and the rail declines horizontal panning.",
    "PRESENTATION no longer keeps a hand-typed second copy of the figure endpoint labels; one of them appeared nowhere in the data. The figure reads story.figure, so the duplicates are deleted rather than corrected.",
    "scopeCss stripped of comments before scoping: it found rules by looking for the next brace, so a banner comment above an @media rule took the whole block down the plain-rule path and shipped the entire phone composition unscoped and inert while the stylesheet on disk was correct.",
    "business-first still carries empty figure labels in src/data/rebuildProof.ts. Wording is owner-held and deliberately unchanged: the obvious phrasing is on the field’s own banned-copy list."
  ],
